  <page_number>185</page_number>
  <running_head>VARIA POEMATA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">EIVSDEM MELISSI</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2">MELOS,</l>
    <l n="3" type="heading" level="2">Ad Amicum quendam.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>SVMMO Iehouæ sacra mea est lyra</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Summi Iehouæ dum cano filium,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Instincta mens sancti calore</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Numinis, alta volat per astra.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Vertumnus haud me lumine adultero,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Pellace nec me voce Glycyrrhoa</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Sub triste Sirenes barathrum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Abripient male pertinacem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Cuicunque cura est dia anima salus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Obturet aures atque oculos dolis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Scylla canina monstra fugi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Providus &amp; Syculam Charybdin.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Speres abyssos irremeabiles,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Euphraste, si quem trux gula gurgitum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Absorpsit, anfractuosve in imam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Præcipitant Styga tortuosi.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Christus reducit solus ab inferis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Quos vult, &amp; alte cum superis locat:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Selegit idem agmen piorum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Primigeni Chaos ante mundi.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Idem tenebris irradians tuis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Caliginosa nubila dissipulit [?]</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Mentis, serenatumque luce</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Ferre dedit super astra pectus.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The large initial S is set as a woodcut-style letter joined to "VMMO", read as SVMMO. Line 22, "dissipulit", is partly unclear in the scan (the letters "ssp" are blurred), so it is marked [?]. Long s is rendered as plain s throughout. Line-initial "Vertumnus" has a spaced capital V. The poem's stanza structure is not separated in print, so it is kept as one paragraph.</notes>
</page>
